  "scope": "# Review \u2014 `1a5d49e539de`\nAssignment: `review-ad11f5c06ca73080`; approved source SHA-256 `cc9524450ef524c7685a084aba5bd9dbba9455934a30af32d55ed62554312d37`.\nDefect \u2192 repair: missing parametric evidence \u2192 built an episode-fixed `symmetry_axis` prototype with canonical `left-right` and proposed `top-bottom` settings.\nProduction status: generator, canonical Racket authority, approval, and training admission are unchanged; the new setting is explicitly `proposed_unapproved`.\nLesson shape: three identifying demonstrations and four distinct queries per episode, all labeled through the matching exact Racket program.\nChecks: 41/41 task tests; 28 retained Racket evaluations across both settings; 24 adversarial episode configurations / 168 pairs with maximum one retry.\nExport check: public IDs hash exact visible bytes; private metadata and query answers are excluded, duplicate visible payloads are rejected.\nTicket 1: reproduced five retained diagnostics plus the schedule warning; current source already contains the repairs, so no shared change is proposed.\nTicket 2: retained a lawful `ignore_singletons` counterexample with ten differing cells and exact Racket parity; positive coverage, not an audit finding.\nRemaining failures: none in the changed scope. Limits: finite retained seeds/settings and bounded probes, not exhaustive support or variant approval.\nDisposition: routine prototype handoff; maintainer attention is required only if promoting the variant into a production API or training set.\n",
